<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction on Tuesday and demand was also down, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	22.74	    -32	     22.56     22.85</p>
<p>91-Day	25.11	    -52	     24.22     25.37</p>
<p>182-Day     26.84	    -49	     26.73     26.96</p>
<p>357-Day     26.83				26.83     26.83</p>
<p>Last week the 364-day paper was assigned at 27.39 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   3.251 bln pesos    3.61</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   3.195 bln pesos    3.55</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   4.850 bln pesos    5.39</p>
<p>357-Day     600 million pesos   3.040 bln pesos    5.07</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.34 compared with 5.28 the week before, on demand of 17.44 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			  11  basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			  26  basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			 12  basis points</p>
<p>    357-Day			 nil basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559. E-mail at robert.kozak@reuters.com</p>
